{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem (parity siblings of the tickets-branch invariant violation)\nTwo more tickets-branch writers bypass the shared store seams and the two-part invariant\n(under the unified write lock + auto-commit/publish), same class as projects_store\n(ticket fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168):\n1. reconcile_helpers._commit_binding_store_snapshot (reconcile_helpers.py:169) commits\n   .bridge_state binding/rotation/link state via raw git_adapter.add + commit. git_adapter\n   imports only rebar._store.gitutil.run_git — it does NOT acquire rebar._store.lock.write_lock,\n   so it races the ticket-CLI _push_tickets_branch() and concurrent GHA commit-back (the\n   exact race the write lock exists to prevent). Its own docstring documents the\n   \"un-committed local copy silently overwritten by a concurrent run\" bug it half-fixes\n   WITHOUT taking the lock.\n2. alert_store._atomic_write (alert_store.py:84) hand-rolls tempfile+os.replace instead of\n   the shared rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write seam.\n\n## Use the EXISTING seams (NO new facade, NO redesign) — same as ticket fea4\n- rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, *, message=...) — commits all\n  pending tracker changes under the unified write lock (+ rebase guard) then pushes.\n- rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write — the shared crash-atomic write.\n\n## Approach\n1. _commit_binding_store_snapshot: replace the lock-bypassing raw git_adapter add/commit\n   with a call to the EXISTING push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch (which stages+commits\n   pending tracker changes under write_lock and pushes). Preserve its fail-open posture (a\n   commit/push failure must still NOT abort the pass — keep the try/except returning False\n   and logging). The existing seam already scopes to pending changes; confirm the binding\n   state files are what gets committed and that its per-file idempotency (bug 1e08) and no-op\n   -when-clean behavior are preserved (commit_and_push is a no-op when the tree is clean).\n2. alert_store._atomic_write -> fsutil.atomic_write. FIRST determine whether the\n   .bridge_state/bridge_alerts files are committed to the tickets branch (GHA commit-back)\n   or local-only scratch: if committed, they are already published by the same commit-back /\n   commit_and_push path (no extra lock work needed here — just the atomic_write swap); if\n   local scratch, fsutil.atomic_write alone suffices. Document the finding.\n\n## Constraints — BEHAVIOR-PRESERVING\nVerify NO functional change: same files committed, same idempotent no-op when nothing\nchanged, same graceful-degradation on git error (fail-open), same serialized bytes for\nalert files. Pin these with tests before/after. Reuse existing seams ONLY — add no new\nhelper.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. _commit_binding_store_snapshot serializes through the unified write lock (via\n   commit_and_push_tickets_branch); behavior otherwise identical (idempotency, fail-open).\n2. alert_store uses fsutil.atomic_write; residency (committed vs scratch) determined +\n   documented; correct existing seam applied.\n3. No functional/behavioral change beyond lock+seam adoption (pinned by tests).\n\n## Sequencing\nDepends on fea4 landing first ONLY to avoid two concurrent edits to the reconciler commit\npath and to inherit the same seam choice. Edits reconcile_helpers.py + alert_store.py\n(+ tests) — disjoint from A/C/D. Rebase onto fea4 before starting."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786807837335017001,"uuid":"94545c14-6508-47d9-b87b-71bde4665566"}